<h1>Delete Your Account</h1>
<p class="muted">How to remove your Chorvix account and the data tied to it.</p>

<h2>Delete it yourself (fastest)</h2>
<p>Sign in, open your <a href="/account">account page</a>, and choose <strong>Delete my account</strong> at the bottom. Type your account email to confirm and it happens right away: your account is removed and you are signed out everywhere. You can review your account and the content tied to it on that page first.</p>

<h2>Or request deletion by email</h2>
<p>Email <a href="mailto:mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com">mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com</a> from the email address on your account and ask us to delete your account. We will delete your account and the data associated with it.</p>

<h2>Deletion is permanent</h2>
<p>Deleting your account permanently removes your account and its associated data. Art you sold stays available to the people who bought it, with your name removed; order and payment records we must keep for our books stay, with your name and email removed from them. This cannot be undone.</p>

<h2>What data do we hold?</h2>
<p>See our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for what data we collect and how it is used.</p>
